<p class="bl-carousel-hint">12 whole pages - scroll sideways for the next, down inside a frame for the rest of the page, or open one at full width</p>

<p>These twelve, and every page below them, come from Sandbox Beta: a test frame that runs with production's switches and gets each release before production does, so its agents, balances, trades and history are testing data, while production itself is still young and nearly empty. Below them, section by section, are 125 pages of the console and 72 of their tabs and opened panels, each in full. Whoever runs a frame from the kit can start a sandbox like it from the console itself, in the MCP Tester view. The <a href="https://docs.theprotocol.cloud/gallery/">gallery on the docs site</a> has these shots and production's. Every page is walked by the console suite, a real browser that signs in, presses the buttons and reads what comes back, on a sandbox frame before each release reaches production (2,400 measured steps at V0639, none failed). To the best of my knowledge, all of it works. I just cannot click through all of it by hand, which is exactly why the suite exists.</p>

