    excerpt: "This is probably the last post before the code base opens, and the code will go out as it is. So this one steps back and looks at what the last ten days changed: what the network says when it is not sure. A screen whose read failed says so instead of drawing a zero. A payment the ledger cannot record does not happen, and says why, on the sandbox for now. A payment whose answer was lost on its way back is answered again under its key instead of being sent twice, and one that comes back comes back whole. The auditor now tells a ledger that is late from one that is wrong, and the production frames have their first members. Also: a few words about who builds this, and the patch notes since the last post.",
