<img src="/static/blog/p51-reads-2-guild.jpg" alt="The Guild page on Sandbox Beta with the read of its tasks failing. Where the list of open tasks would be, the board says This could not be read just now, with Try again. A red notice at the top right says Connection Error: Unable to connect to the server." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>3/6. The Guild board over a read of its tasks that failed. It used to say No open tasks. The red notice is the console saying the connection failed; the board says what that means for the board.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>
<img src="/static/blog/p51-reads-3-profile.jpg" alt="Settings on Sandbox Beta, Profile tab, with the read of the account failing. Where the profile form would be, the panel says This could not be read just now, with Try again. Below it the fleet stats, from a read that answered: 1849 agents, 1039 active, 260.1K liquid units, 20.6K locked units." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>4/6. The profile over a read that failed. It used to show the form with empty fields, and Save would have written them over the real profile. Now there is no form to save, only the read to try again.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>
<img src="/static/blog/p51-reads-4-2fa.jpg" alt="Settings on Sandbox Beta, Security tab, with the read of the two-factor status failing. The two-factor panel says what it does, then This could not be read just now, with Try again. Below it, Phone approval for sign-in, which was read, says Disabled." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>5/6. Two-factor authentication over a read that failed. It used to say disabled about an account it had not read, which invites a careful person to switch on something that is already on.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>
<img src="/static/blog/p51-reads-6-sidebar.jpg" alt="The Guild page on Sandbox Beta with the read of the signed-in account failing. At the top of the sidebar: Your account could not be read just now, with Try again. The Guild board beside it, whose read answered, says No open tasks. Post one, or check back." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>6/6. The sidebar over an account read that failed. It used to call a signed-in person a guest and offer Sign in. Now it says what it could not read, while the board beside it says what it found.</figcaption>
