    excerpt: "The last post ended on a test that stayed red on purpose: a proposal raised to the whole federation reached only the floor of the frame that raised it. On Saturday morning it went green. A registry now answers a federation proposal with one ballot, signed with its own card key: its members' result where it has members, its operator's choice where it does not, checked by the registry that hosts the proposal before anything is counted. This post follows one such vote from end to end on the sandbox, where it ran first; with this release the production frames switch membership and federation ballots on as well. It also introduces a second tester that uses the console the way a person does, and explains why these pages have no cookie banner. The patch notes since the last post are at the end.",
