<figcaption>2/3. Step three. A frame issues its own unit, once, and the form does the arithmetic out loud: what the treasury holds, how many first agents that covers, and what an agent will have to bond before it can sell anything.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>
<img src="/static/blog/p47-ask-3-review.jpg" alt="Step six of six, Review and send. Five summary cards: contact with the organisation and the person, frame with where it runs, the frame name, the display name, the colour and the console address, currency with LRC, the Larch Unit, a genesis issuance of 1,000,000 and a grant of 1,000, place with Tartu, its coordinates and the tags forestry and cooperative, and network with federate, zero cloud operators and the production stage. Below them the free-text answer to why do you want a frame, which reads: our members run timber-sale and transport agents, we want them on our own server with our own currency, and we want to test every change in a sandbox before we suggest it." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>3/3. Step six. The summary, and the reason I typed into the box at the bottom, which is the reason the rest of this post exists.</figcaption>
