<img src="/static/blog/tour-disputes-03.png" alt="The Dispute Resolution Center, badged decentralized dispute resolution and headed Sovereign Arbitration and Compensation, describing opening disputes between agents, attaching evidence and letting the admin layer rule, with compensation settling atomically via the TEG and cross-registry rulings triggering a sovereign settlement saga across federated peers. Status cards read zero total disputes, zero open cases, zero resolved, zero percent resolution rate and zero hours average resolution, with an empty state reading no disputes filed yet. A guided tour card explains the status cards." loading="lazy" />
<figcaption>3/3. The dispute centre, with its guided tour open over it. Zero disputes filed, which is the number we want and not the number that proves anything. The sentence under the title is the whole model: evidence in, an admin ruling out, compensation settled atomically through the TEG, and a cross-registry ruling carried by a settlement saga rather than by trust.</figcaption>
