<button type="button" class="bl-car-btn bl-car-next" data-car="next" aria-label="Next frame">&rsaquo;</button>
</div>
<p class="bl-carousel-hint">3 frames - scroll sideways</p>

<p>One thing is planned rather than built, and it is the part that decides whether any of this survives contact with real commerce. Not every dispute can be public. Some settlements will carry terms that neither party may publish, and the naive fix, leaving those entries out, is exactly the fix that destroys the property the record has. A hash chain with holes in it is not a chain. So the plan is attestation instead of omission: publish the signed digest of the withheld entry and its link to the previous one, keep the content private, and let anyone still verify that nothing was inserted, removed or reordered between two things they can read. Confidential in content, unbroken in sequence. The chain does not care what the entry says, only that it cannot be quietly changed later.</p>

<h2>How we know the surface still works</h2>

<p>Everything above is a claim about a running system, so it is worth showing the thing that argues with those claims every night. The MCP tester sweeps both bridges end to end: 421 public tools plus 317 admin tools, and it holds every one of them to a twelve-axis contract rather than to a status code. HTTP status, response shape, value types, read-after-write side effect, EventStore emission, audit-log row, tier-set membership, wrong-tier rejection, cross-frame parity, wrapper against route schema drift, a per-tool latency baseline, and an eventual-consistency budget. On top of that sit 86 multi-step lifecycles, 77 public and 9 admin, which chain real mutations, transfer, lock, dispute, governance, cross-frame, and then prove the side effects round-trip.</p>

<p>Two rules matter more than the percentage. Skips count against the pass rate, because a skip is a coverage hole and not a victory. And the sweep is always proxied to a sandbox registry: the target is fixed inside the runner, so even if every other layer were bypassed the sweep still lands in sandbox containers. Production is never the thing being written to.</p>

<div class="bl-carousel-wrap">
<button type="button" class="bl-car-btn bl-car-prev" data-car="prev" aria-label="Previous frame">&lsaquo;</button>
