<p>The honest framing: this is not finished. Tests are not fully fixed yet, the tester is still being built out, and it is already good enough that we would not want to ship without it. The reason it needs constant attention is the same reason it exists. The system moves fast, most days carry new images, and a test suite that is not updated at that pace stops describing the thing it is pointed at. So the sandbox tier stays up on purpose, to run the sweep nightly against whatever was built that day.</p>

<p>One consequence worth naming, because someone will hit it. The guided tours work with or without the sandbox tier running. The tutorials that pay out do not, and that is deliberate rather than broken: tutorial payouts belong in a sandbox ledger, because running them against production would pollute a real ledger with teaching money. Those are being repaired next week.</p>

<h2>A note about the silence</h2>

<p>The gap between posts was not a content strategy. Life picked this quarter to stage a controlled burn, and the word doing the most work in that sentence is <em>controlled</em>. I have been heads down mostly because heads down is the one direction with a decent view at the moment, and because a ledger that has to balance to zero every time anyone looks turns out to be restful company when very little else will hold still.</p>

<p>So, sorry for the quiet. It was triage rather than disinterest. This is one person with a finite number of hours and a famously clumsy pair of hands, and when the choice is between writing about the work and doing the work, the work wins and the writing turns up late, in a heap, slightly out of breath. Thank you for still being here. The sweep runs nightly whether or not I manage to.</p>

<h2>Patchnotes</h2>

<p>The last post left the fleet at V0212. What follows is <strong>V0213 through V0285</strong>, eight days, supply delta zero on every frame throughout.</p>

<h3>Frames</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>EU</strong> is live. Brussels, currency ECU.</li>
<li><strong>ASIA</strong> is live. Singapore, currency ACU.</li>
<li>Two cloud operators per frame: Amsterdam, Lisbon, Shenzhen, Ho Chi Minh City.</li>
<li>A joining frame now receives a federation licence from the frame that admits it, issued inside the admitting transaction.</li>
<li>Operators and frames draw licences from one table. A key presented on the wrong class of rail is refused.</li>
<li>A planned frame can hold its licence before its first boot.</li>
<li>Provisioning runs under purpose-named service accounts. The founder account onboards nothing.</li>
<li>System agents no longer appear in discovery by default.</li>
<li>The standup driver is a single resumable pass.</li>
<li>Registry cards publish their real federation address instead of an internal name.</li>
<li>A frame refuses to provision operators while running on a mock identity.</li>
<li>Frame licence management in the console, with unlicensed peers named on screen.</li>
