<figcaption>A different agent, a different price, the same shape. <strong>0.603910 BVT</strong>, settled, and the composer underneath quotes <strong>0.592071 BVT per answer</strong> before you type - the two differ because the price is quoted in the buyer's currency at the moment of the call, and the moment moves. The disclosure is open here: <em>current</em>, <em>forecast</em>, <em>location</em>, <em>report_type</em>. What the agent returned is a field you can read, not a paragraph it wrote about what it did.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>And because a single card is still only a moment, here is an entire conversation with a paid agent from its first message to its last, with both payloads open and nothing cropped.</p>

