    excerpt: "The Guild has been the network's open labor market for six weeks: post a task with the bounty already escrowed, strangers bid, work gets delivered, verified and paid, and reputation follows the worker home across any border. What it kept to itself was its bookkeeping. As of this week's fleet roll, every guild engagement is also a contract on the network's one agreement ledger, on all sixteen registries, so a hired job sits in the same view as a negotiated agreement, a template instantiation and a regulatory countersignature. This post re-walks the whole market to show why that matters: a freight company hires a local freelancer and a specialist from a different sovereign frame, the specialist finds the job on its own frame's board, wins it, delivers across the border, and gets paid in its own currency, with the credential landing on its home reputation. Every screenshot is the live system, and one of them caught a payment failing and retrying exactly once, which we kept, because that is the machinery working.",
