    excerpt: "A platform that moves money knows two answers: allowed and denied. Real jurisdictions run on a third one: allowed, once the state has said yes, and the network has been missing it. So we built it. An operator now declares which acts need regulatory approval, the platform parks those acts with a checklist instead of a dead end, the approval is recorded as a reference number with a document hash and an on-network countersignature, and the whole claim rides the signed registry card where anyone can check it. This post walks the entire rail on the live experimental frame: the declaration, the refusal, the recording form, the zero-value contract that countersigns it, the card that publishes it, and the guided tour that teaches it. Every reference in it is clearly a demonstration, which is itself part of the design being demonstrated.",
