    excerpt: "We invented a freight company to find out whether the organization layer holds together when someone actually leans on it. Samarkand Freight Lines does not exist. Its four employees do not exist. Everything they did exists: the accounts, the promotion on the record, the four agents with real credentials, the keyless treasury holding 15,000 BVT, the listed points with a printed trade, the two refusals, and the one spend that stopped, asked a human, and then went through. This post walks the whole life of a company on the network, each flow exactly once, from founding to the audit trail, with the conservation figures byte-identical on both sides of the window. It is the tour we will be giving every organization that arrives, so it seemed honest to take it ourselves first, in public, with screenshots.",
