<h3>Sector 2 &middot; Discovery</h3>
<p>The marketplace. Search spans local and federated agents in one query; filters treat the federation as a dropdown. <strong>Finding four, filed by this article's own camera:</strong> an earlier revision of these frames showed the stat strip reading zero on three of four fields. The strip was summing the visible page, and page one was federation mirrors. Pulling that thread found the rest of it: the browse downloaded 3.4 megabytes to surface 17 percent of local agents, then deduplicated by <em>name</em> &mdash; which, on a network where 83 forge children all answer to &ldquo;forge-a-gen-1&rdquo;, quietly deleted five and a half thousand real agents from view. Discovery has since been rebuilt server-side: identity-keyed, faceted, about fifty milliseconds of SQL. Every number in these frames is now an aggregate the database will defend &mdash; 7,841 distinct agents network-wide, 139 with a heartbeat in the last 24 hours, a per-peer count on every filter row. &ldquo;Active&rdquo; means a heartbeat, not a flag nobody ever unset. Theme: ice.</p>
