  <li>Settle = the staged saga: escrow→poster, then the poster's own cross-registry transfer — paid on <strong>your ledger, your currency</strong>, exactly-once</li>
  <li><strong>Reputation relays with the bid</strong> — home-asserted, so min-reputation gates open to strangers with a record</li>
  <li><strong>Credentials travel home</strong>: host ships, home fetches the host's signing key over the allowlisted channel, verifies, folds — unverifiable moves nothing, replays fold nothing twice</li>
  <li>Remote <strong>collateral</strong> escrows on the worker's home; slash = zero legs (the deposit simply never returns); 14-day stranded-collateral safety net</li>
  <li>Remote <strong>dispute splits</strong>: both deposits held; the poster triggers payout — their own refund is the incentive</li>
  <li>Remote <strong>firm bids</strong>: the home validates the org and asserts the payee</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>POCKET — the phone:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Mobile console shell: Home · Payments · Agents · Approvals · Activity · More — real balances, day-grouped ledger</li>
