    excerpt: "There are sixteen sovereign registries on this network, each its own little country with its own admin panel, and until this week running all of them meant sixteen tabs and a prayer. Now there is one screen. The Galactic Command Center is a star map of the entire federation, and clicking a star commands that registry — fund a treasury, suspend an agent, fire a probe, restart the operator's whole stack — through a relay that means the browser never once goes cross-origin. The map is the interface. Restart an operator and you watch its star dim and pulse until it comes back healthy; I proved it by restarting Sydney for real and timing the recovery at thirty-four seconds. The supply invariant for all three frames now sits permanently at the top of the screen, read from an independent auditor, and there is a second cockpit surface: a literal planet, where the same Bridge commands fly off a spinning Earth. The single most important thing about the whole cockpit is still the thing it cannot do: it adds zero new ways to move money, so Δ=0 holds by construction. I also made the maps cinematic, because it was three in the morning and the topology was already correct.",
