<p>The orange-highlighted phases are the Phase F bug-finder layer shipped this week; everything else has been load-bearing since Phase D earlier the same day. The dotted lateral arrows out of Phase 4 are the per-call verifier stack &mdash; the seven base axes plus the new F.5 eventual-consistency poll &mdash; firing on every single mutation lifecycle. The same diagram and a full per-axis operating reference live in the Oracle docs at <a href="/ui#/docs/12" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chapter 12 &mdash; MCP Integration</a>; if you want the click-through for every probe envelope shape, the wrapper authoring guide, and the audit-pipe details, that's the surface to land on.</p>

